 @alexw.michelsen2365  The memory thing is misleading. I hoghly recommend GN's vid, which explains it.

When you play a game and it allocates the full 11 gigabytes of a 1080 ti, it doesn't actually use them. It just keeps them at the ready. The extra bandwidth of GDDR6X more than makes up for the smaller total amount of VRam. Consider that the 1080 Ti has 11 gigs vram and the 3080 runs 90-100% faster than that on 4k with 10 gb Vram.

Mind you, I only found out the same recently.

